# task 07 string_append — expected output: 1000000 #
# build: none (interpreter)    run: a68g 07_string_append.a68 #
# note: a STRING is a FLEX ROW CHAR, and +:= allocates a new row and copies the old #
# note: one, so the loop is quadratic by design, the same shape as the C row realloc #
# note: plus strcat. Left at a million because ten times the count is a hundred times #
# note: the work. #
# note: measured cost of that quadratic loop in this interpreter: 300000 appends take #
# note: about 6 minutes, so the full million is roughly an hour. Nothing is cut off for #
# note: being slow; this is the row's second slowest task after task 10. #

STRING text := "";

FOR i FROM 1 TO 1000000 DO
  text +:= "x"
OD;

print((whole(UPB text, 0), newline))
